# * pair in CSV rules: this repo's extension, not upstream's

# ** 1. A transfer between two of our accounts is two records with the same date and
# time. The Source record's pair rule joins its Destination as row 2, making one
# transaction; a Destination without a Source converts on its own; other records
# are untouched.
<
2026-09-30,09:24:50,5678,Internal Transfer,Source,-1000.00
2026-09-30,08:14:21,1234,Internal Transfer,Destination,1000.00
2026-09-30,09:24:50,1234,Internal Transfer,Destination,1000.00
2026-10-01,12:00:00,1234,Purchase,,-40.00
RULES
fields date, time, acct, type, side, amount
if,let:account
%acct 1234,joint
%acct 5678,personal

account1 assets:bank:%{account}
amount1 %amount
if %side Source
  pair %date %time
  description transfer to %{to}
  account2 assets:bank:%{to}
  amount2 %amount_2
if,let:to
%acct_2 1234,joint
%acct_2 5678,personal

if %side Destination
  description from outside
  account2 equity:outside

$ ./csvtest.sh
2026-09-30 transfer to joint
    assets:bank:personal                       -1000.00
    assets:bank:joint                           1000.00

2026-09-30 from outside
    assets:bank:joint                           1000.00
    equity:outside                             -1000.00

2026-10-01
    assets:bank:joint                            -40.00
    expenses:unknown                              40.00

>=0

# ** 2. The partner may come before its initiator in the file. An initiator with no
# partner converts alone, its row 2 fields empty, which a block can test.
<
2026-09-30,09:24:50,1234,Destination,1000.00
2026-09-30,09:24:50,5678,Source,-1000.00
2026-10-02,10:00:00,5678,Source,-250.00
RULES
fields date, time, acct, side, amount
account1 assets:%acct
amount1 %amount
if %side Source
  pair %date %time
  description to %acct_2
  account2 assets:%acct_2
  amount2 %amount_2
if %side Source
& !%acct_2 .
  description to outside
  account2 expenses:transfers

$ ./csvtest.sh
2026-09-30 to 1234
    assets:5678                                -1000.00
    assets:1234                                 1000.00

2026-10-02 to outside
    assets:5678                                 -250.00
    expenses:transfers                           250.00

>=0

# ** 3. A record is a partner once, for the first initiator in the file; a record with
# a pair rule of its own is never a partner, so two Sources do not pair each other.
<
2026-09-30,09:24:50,A,Source,-100.00
2026-09-30,09:24:50,B,Source,-100.00
2026-09-30,09:24:50,C,Destination,100.00
RULES
fields date, time, acct, side, amount
account1 assets:%acct
amount1 %amount
if %side Source
  pair %date %time
  account2 assets:%acct_2
  amount2 %amount_2

$ ./csvtest.sh
2026-09-30
    assets:A                                    -100.00
    assets:C                                     100.00

2026-09-30
    assets:B                                    -100.00
    assets:                                      100.00

>=0

# ** 4. Pairing follows merging: a merged group can be the partner, its rows becoming
# rows 2 and 3.
<
2026-01-05,A,out,-100.00
2026-01-05,B,in,90.00
2026-01-05,B,fee,10.00
RULES
fields date, acct, side, amount
account1 assets:%acct
amount1 %amount
if %side in
  merge
if %side out
  pair %date
  account2 assets:%acct_2
  amount2 %amount_2
  account3 expenses:fees
  amount3 %amount_3

$ ./csvtest.sh
2026-01-05
    assets:A                                    -100.00
    assets:B                                      90.00
    expenses:fees                                 10.00

>=0

# ** 5. A pair rule needs a key.
<
2026-01-05,A,-1
RULES
fields date, acct, amount
account1 %acct
if A
  pair

$ ./csvtest.sh
>2
hledger: Error: input.rules: pair rule needs a value: the fields that identify the other record of the pair, eg "pair %date %time"
>=1

# ** 6. An error in a paired transaction cites the initiator's line and shows both rows.
<
2026-09-30,09:24:50,A,Source,-100.00
2026-09-30,09:24:50,B,Destination,90.00
RULES
fields date, time, acct, side, amount
account1 assets:%acct
amount1 %amount
if %side Source
  pair %date %time
  account2 assets:%acct_2
  amount2 %amount_2

$ ./csvtest.sh
>2 /input:1:
1 \| 2026-09-30
  \|     assets:A                                    -100\.00
  \|     assets:B                                      90\.00

This transaction is unbalanced\.
The real postings' sum should be 0 but is -10\.00
  -100\.00  \+  90\.00  =  -10\.00
this entry was converted from:
record: 2026-09-30,09:24:50,A,Source,-100\.00,2026-09-30,09:24:50,B,Destination,90\.00
row 1:
  %1 date    2026-09-30
  %2 time    09:24:50
  %3 acct    A
  %4 side    Source
  %5 amount  -100\.00
row 2:
  %1_2 date_2    2026-09-30
  %2_2 time_2    09:24:50
  %3_2 acct_2    B
  %4_2 side_2    Destination
  %5_2 amount_2  90\.00/
>=1

# ** 7. A pair rule's block that matches on a later row's field can never pair, and
# says so, as a merge rule's does.
<
2026-09-30,A,-1
2026-09-30,B,1
RULES
fields date, acct, amount
account1 assets:%acct
amount1 %amount
if %acct_2 B
  pair %date

$ ./csvtest.sh
2026-09-30
    assets:A                                      -1
    expenses:unknown                               1

2026-09-30
    assets:B                                       1
    income:unknown                                -1

>2 /^Warning: input.rules: an if block containing a pair rule matches on a later row's field \(%acct_2\); this can not trigger a pair, since these fields are empty until after pairing$/
>=0
